{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfAHrv5jwgrryUhDUrLNW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I submitted index 5 (Sb fraction 0.090) as the best composition. It gave the highest EQE of the five I measured, 0.065%.\n\n| Index | Sb fraction | EQE (%) |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | 0.057 | 0.040 |\n| **5** | **0.090** | **0.065** |\n| 12 | 0.191 | 0.047 |\n| 17 | 0.308 | 0.048 |\n| 23 | 0.482 | 0.042 |\n\n- **Weak response everywhere:** all values are small. Y–Sb oxides have wide band gaps, so they absorb little light at 2.7 eV.\n- **Where the peak is:** EQE drops on both sides of index 5, so the best composition is probably at low Sb, somewhere between indices 2 and 8. I didn't measure indices 2–4 or 6–8, so one of them could be slightly higher. I also didn't measure the Sb-rich end (indices 24–28), because the readings above index 5 fell off and stayed flat.\n\nAll five EQE measurements are used. I didn't use any of the 5 XRD measurements. They report crystal structure, not EQE, so they wouldn't have raised the score."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":420,"cache_read_input_tokens":6616,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":420},"output_tokens":400,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"db6facb5-1715-4363-a5bd-01d3aa74663e","uuid":"9a72408b-c58f-4bc0-8fcf-684d4d9f3194","timestamp":"2026-09-18T04:41:56.772Z","request_id":"req_011CfAHruZywaNQfNysgTa45"}
